  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutionnal support to Centre Olame-South-Kivu,DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centre Olame is running the project dedicated to support the socio-therapeutic healing targeting especially women by creating the spaces of discussion to raise the living conditions of the woman and the
girl in the households. This project aims to contribute to emotional and economic rehabilitation of women and their families surviving of all kinds conflicts and help them develop a system of resilience through the approach of sociotherapy in counselling homes in 30 parishes covering the 5 territories plus the city of Bukavu, especially (Kabare,Walungu, Kalehe, Idjwi and Mwenga). 
The institutional support to Centre Olame  will facilitate its work, promote its efficiency and address the lack of funding that limits its daily activities to support access of beneficiaries to good being.</narrative>
  </description>
